v2 page twins live here, mirroring the v1 filenames at the dashboard root.

A file dropped in here as `<name>.html` is served instead of `<root>/<name>.html`
to any user whose interface resolves to v2. Nothing else is required — no route
change, no registration. A page with no file here silently serves v1, which is
why partial migration is always in a shippable state.

Deleting one file here = rollback layer 3 (one page, all users).
Deleting this directory = rollback layer 4 (all of v2).

Empty in phase 0 BY DESIGN: the phase-0 gate is that every page is byte-identical
with the toggle in either position, which is only provable with no twins present.
